  "description": "Joins Rask.Sync's merge engine to an object-storage bucket so several devices can share data with no server between them. Each client appends to a prefix only it writes, so there are no write conflicts to resolve; peers are discovered with a grouped listing and read forward from a per-peer watermark, so syncing costs what changed rather than what exists. Edits made offline queue locally and flush on the next sync, and the whole thing reports a status — synced, pending, offline, conflicts — that a UI can render.",
